<title>USA: Lexmark hires business printers manager. [CORRECTED 20:36 GMT]</title>
<headline>Lexmark hires business printers manager. [CORRECTED 20:36 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Ky. 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lexmark International Group Inc said John C. Mitchell has joined the company as vice president and general manager of the Business Printer Division, a new position at Lexmark International.</p>
<p>(Company corrects details of Mitchell's appointment)</p>
<p>Mitchell, will be responsible for Lexmark's largest operating division, serving users of networked laser printers worldwide.  He will report to Paul J. Curlander, executive vice president of operations.</p>
<p>Mitchell was president of the $1.1 billion Planters and LifeSavers companies at RJR Nabisco Holdings Corp's Nabisco Holdings Corp affiliate.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.))</p>
